          "instruction": "Read the article and answer.",
          "title": "The 36 questions",
          "text": "Can you fall in love with a stranger by asking questions? In a famous experiment, a psychologist asked pairs of strangers to ask each other 36 personal questions. They started with easy ones, like 'What would be a perfect day for you?' and moved to more personal ones, like 'What are you most grateful for?' At the end, they looked into each other's eyes for four minutes. Six months later, one couple got married!\n\nThe experiment shows that asking good questions — and really listening to the answers — helps people feel closer.",
